cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article that
  introduces the protocol.
title: "treatment-identity: verify that the treatment an experiment declares is the one its data loader delivers"
abstract: >-
  Seven CPU treatment-delivery gates probe the loader output declared by an
  experiment, including finite numerical ranges and channel-content contracts.
  Content guards can also run immediately after collation and before model
  invocation. A separate geometry gate checks evaluation integrity, and
  treatment separability uses matched seeds plus a paired distributional test.
  Certificates remain bounded observations rather than claims about
  optimisation correctness.
